In Chromium, enabling Certificate Transparency (kCertificateTransparencyAskBeforeEnabling,
which Vanadium's 0244 turns on) also enables SCT auditing on desktop: with Safe
Browsing on, samples of visited sites' certificates/SCTs are checked with or
reported to Google (hashdance lookups, or full reports with extended reporting).
Vanadium doesn't get this, as Android never enables SCT auditing. Keep it off,
so enforcing CT sends nothing new to Google.

--- a/chrome/browser/ssl/sct_reporting_service.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ssl/sct_reporting_service.cc
@@ -215,11 +215,10 @@
 SCTReportingService::~SCTReportingService() = default;
 
 network::mojom::SCTAuditingMode SCTReportingService::GetReportingMode() {
+  // SCT auditing sends samples of the certificates of visited sites to Google
+  // (with Safe Browsing on). Keep it off, as on Android, also when Certificate
+  // Transparency enforcement is enabled.
   bool is_sct_auditing_enabled = false;
-#if !BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
-  is_sct_auditing_enabled =
-      SystemNetworkContextManager::IsCertificateTransparencyEnabled();
-#endif
   if (profile_->IsOffTheRecord() || !is_sct_auditing_enabled) {
     return network::mojom::SCTAuditingMode::kDisabled;
   }
